{"step_index":585,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-21T23:55:51Z","thinking":"**Identifying a Bug**\n\nOkay, I've hit a snag. It seems there's a bug in `viewProcess`. I'm starting to suspect the issue revolves around how `data.stats` is being handled. I need to trace the return value from `get_process_details` and double-check how the raw DB row is being processed. The backend function seems fine in isolation, it's just returning the database row.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"replace_file_content","args":{"AllowMultiple":false,"Description":"Fix viewProcess data mapping","EndLine":1434,"Instruction":"Map the DB output fields to the stats fields expected by loadResults","ReplacementContent":"async function viewProcess(processId) {\n    try {\n        const dataStr = await window.pywebview.api.get_process_details(processId);\n        const data = JSON.parse(dataStr);\n        if (!data || !data.id) throw new Error(\"لم يتم العثور على العملية\");\n        \n        currentProcessId = processId;\n        const stats = {\n            total: data.total_shortages || 0,\n            matched: data.matched_count || 0,\n            not_found: data.not_found_count || 0,\n            review: data.review_count || 0\n        };\n        loadResults(stats);\n        window.showScreen('screen-results');\n    } catch (error) {\n        showToast('تعذر تحميل تفاصيل العملية', 'error');\n        console.error(error);\n    }\n}","StartLine":1423,"TargetContent":"async function viewProcess(processId) {\n    try {\n        const dataStr = await window.pywebview.api.get_process_details(processId);\n        const data = JSON.parse(dataStr);\n        currentProcessId = processId;\n        loadResults(data.stats || {});\n        window.showScreen('screen-results');\n    } catch (error) {\n        showToast('تعذر تحميل تفاصيل العملية', 'error');\n    }\n}","TargetFile":"d:\\AI_Engineer\\Pharmacy-agy\\desktop_app\\templates\\index.html","toolAction